INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_16',
  'What is a primary benefit of adopting Infrastructure as Code (IaC) practices for managing cloud resources?',
  'mcq',
  '["It allows for manual, ad-hoc changes to infrastructure without tracking.","It ensures consistency and repeatability in infrastructure deployments.","It eliminates the need for any form of version control system.","It requires infrastructure changes to be approved only by the operations team."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) highlights a primary benefit of IaC: ensuring consistency and repeatability. By defining infrastructure in code, deployments become standardized, reducing configuration drift and human error. Option A is incorrect because IaC discourages manual, ad-hoc changes, promoting changes through code. Option C is incorrect as version control is a fundamental aspect and benefit of IaC, allowing tracking of changes and collaboration. Option D is incorrect because IaC promotes collaboration across teams (DevOps), not limiting approval to a single team.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  1,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_17',
  'Which characteristic of Infrastructure as Code (IaC) is directly supported by integrating configuration files with a version control system?',
  'mcq',
  '["Reduced need for peer review processes.","Automatic scaling of infrastructure resources.","Enhanced collaboration and auditability of changes.","Exclusive control over infrastructure by a single administrator."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) accurately describes how version control systems enhance IaC. They enable teams to collaborate effectively, track every change made to infrastructure definitions, and provide an audit trail for compliance and troubleshooting. Option A is incorrect because version control facilitates peer review by making changes visible and reviewable. Option B is unrelated to the direct benefits of version control for IaC. Option D is incorrect as IaC, especially with version control, promotes shared ownership and collaborative management, moving away from single-point-of-failure administration.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  2,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_18',
  'A development team frequently needs to provision identical testing environments for new feature branches. Which benefit of Infrastructure as Code (IaC) is most relevant to this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Increased reliance on manual configuration steps.","The ability to provision infrastructure with unique, undocumented settings each time.","Ensuring repeatability and consistency across multiple environment deployments.","Delegating all infrastructure management to the cloud provider''s console."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) directly addresses the scenario. IaC''s repeatability ensures that the same code can be used to provision identical environments reliably, which is crucial for testing. Option A is incorrect because IaC aims to reduce, not increase, manual configuration. Option B is contrary to IaC principles, which promote documented and consistent configurations. Option D is incorrect as IaC is about managing infrastructure programmatically, reducing direct reliance on manual console operations.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  3,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_19',
  'In the context of Infrastructure as Code (IaC), what does the term ''documentation as code'' primarily refer to?',
  'mcq',
  '["Writing detailed external documentation for every infrastructure component.","Using code comments as the sole source of operational instructions.","The IaC configuration files themselves serving as up-to-date infrastructure documentation.","Generating automated reports on infrastructure costs from code."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) defines ''documentation as code'' in IaC. The declarative nature of IaC means that the configuration files explicitly describe the desired state of the infrastructure, making them a reliable and often self-documenting source of truth. Option A is incorrect because while external documentation can exist, ''documentation as code'' emphasizes the code itself. Option B is too narrow; while comments are useful, the entire configuration serves as documentation. Option D is a separate benefit related to cost management, not directly ''documentation as code''.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  4,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_20',
  'Which of the following is a direct benefit of using Infrastructure as Code (IaC) to manage infrastructure changes?',
  'mcq',
  '["Increased likelihood of configuration drift between environments.","Slower deployment cycles due to extensive manual checks.","Reduced human error and improved reliability of deployments.","Elimination of the need for any form of testing infrastructure."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is a key benefit of IaC. By automating infrastructure provisioning and management through code, human error is significantly reduced, leading to more reliable and consistent deployments. Option A is incorrect because IaC helps prevent configuration drift by enforcing a desired state. Option B is incorrect as IaC typically leads to faster and more efficient deployment cycles. Option D is incorrect; IaC makes testing infrastructure changes easier and more repeatable, but it does not eliminate the need for testing.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  5,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_21',
  'A team is adopting IaC to manage their infrastructure. They want to ensure that any change to the infrastructure is reviewed by at least one other team member before being applied. Which IaC benefit directly supports this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Reduced operational overhead by eliminating all review processes.","The ability to treat infrastructure configuration as code, enabling peer review via version control.","Automatic deployment of all changes without human intervention.","Exclusive control of infrastructure changes by a single lead architect."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) directly supports the requirement for peer review. By managing infrastructure as code and storing it in a version control system, changes can be submitted as pull requests and reviewed by other team members before being merged and applied, just like application code. Option A is incorrect; IaC streamlines processes but doesn''t eliminate necessary reviews. Option C is incorrect; while automation is key, review processes are often integrated. Option D is contrary to the collaborative nature of IaC and version control.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  6,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_22',
  'A company wants to ensure that their development, staging, and production environments are identical in terms of infrastructure configuration. Which IaC benefit is most critical for achieving this goal?',
  'mcq',
  '["Manual configuration to allow for environment-specific tweaks.","The ability to use different IaC tools for each environment.","Consistency and repeatability of infrastructure deployments.","Relying solely on cloud provider default settings for all environments."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is the most critical benefit. IaC allows defining infrastructure once and deploying it repeatedly across different environments, ensuring they are consistent and identical, which helps prevent ''it works on my machine'' issues. Option A is incorrect; manual tweaks introduce inconsistencies. Option B is incorrect; using different tools can introduce inconsistencies and increase complexity. Option D is incorrect; relying on defaults might not meet specific application requirements and doesn''t guarantee consistency if defaults change or are overridden.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  7,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'easy'
);

