  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is a direct outcome of IaC automation. By automating provisioning, deployments become faster, more consistent, and less prone to human error, leading to increased reliability. Option A is incorrect; IaC reduces manual configuration time. Option B is incorrect; IaC often enables faster recovery through automated redeployment. Option D is incorrect; IaC aims to reduce human error.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  8,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_24',
  'Which benefit of Infrastructure as Code (IaC) is most relevant for a team that needs to quickly roll back to a previous known good configuration after a failed deployment?',
  'mcq',
  '["The ability to manually reconfigure each resource individually.","Enhanced collaboration and auditability through version control.","Reduced need for testing environments due to automated deployments.","The inherent complexity of managing infrastructure through code."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is highly relevant. By storing infrastructure configurations in version control, teams can easily revert to a previous commit (a known good configuration) and redeploy it, enabling quick rollbacks and disaster recovery. Option A is incorrect; manual reconfiguration is slow and error-prone. Option C is incorrect; IaC makes testing easier, but doesn''t eliminate its need. Option D is incorrect; while there''s an initial learning curve, IaC aims to simplify management in the long run.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  9,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_25',
  'Which of the following is a core benefit of adopting Infrastructure as Code (IaC) practices with Terraform?',
  'mcq',
  '["Increased consistency and repeatability in infrastructure deployments.","Elimination of the need for version control systems for infrastructure configurations.","Reduced complexity by requiring manual approval for every infrastructure change.","Exclusive support for single-cloud environments, simplifying management."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) highlights a primary benefit of IaC: by defining infrastructure in code, deployments become consistent and repeatable, reducing human error and ensuring environments are identical across stages. Option B (incorrect) is a misconception; IaC thrives on version control systems (like Git) to track changes, enable collaboration, and facilitate rollbacks. Option C (incorrect) describes a process that would increase, not reduce, complexity and operational overhead, contradicting IaC''s goal of automation. Option D (incorrect) is false; Terraform is well-known for its multi-cloud and hybrid-cloud capabilities, not for exclusive single-cloud support.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  10,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_26',
  'A development team uses Terraform to manage their cloud infrastructure. They want to ensure that all infrastructure changes are reviewed by peers before deployment. Which IaC benefit does this directly support?',
  'mcq',
  '["Peer review and collaboration through version control.","Automatic drift detection without manual intervention.","Guaranteed zero downtime deployments for all resources.","Simplified migration to a new cloud provider."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is a direct benefit of IaC. By storing infrastructure definitions in version control systems (like Git), teams can leverage standard code review processes (peer review) for infrastructure changes, improving quality and collaboration. Option B (incorrect) is a benefit of IaC, but it''s not the primary mechanism for peer review. Option C (incorrect) is an aspirational goal often achieved with specific deployment strategies, but not an inherent guarantee of IaC itself. Option D (incorrect) is a potential long-term benefit of Terraform''s multi-cloud abstraction, but not directly related to peer review of changes.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  11,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_27',
  'Which of the following is NOT considered a direct benefit of using Infrastructure as Code (IaC) with Terraform?',
  'mcq',
  '["Elimination of all security vulnerabilities in deployed infrastructure.","Improved consistency and reduced configuration drift.","Enhanced collaboration and peer review through version control.","Faster and more reliable infrastructure provisioning."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is not a direct benefit of IaC. While IaC can help enforce security best practices and make security auditing easier, it does not inherently eliminate all security vulnerabilities, as vulnerabilities can still exist in the code itself, in underlying services, or in configuration choices. Option B (incorrect) is a key benefit, as IaC ensures environments are built consistently and helps detect when manual changes cause ''drift'' from the defined state. Option C (incorrect) is a significant benefit, as IaC configurations stored in version control enable standard code review workflows. Option D (incorrect) is also a core benefit, as automation leads to quicker and more dependable deployments compared to manual processes.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  12,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_28',
  'A team is struggling with inconsistent environments between their development and staging environments. Which benefit of Infrastructure as Code (IaC) with Terraform directly addresses this issue?',
  'mcq',
  '["Repeatability and consistency of infrastructure deployments.","Automatic cost optimization across all cloud resources.","Real-time monitoring and alerting for infrastructure health.","Simplified application development and debugging."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) directly addresses the problem of inconsistent environments. IaC ensures that the same code defines and provisions infrastructure across different environments (dev, staging, production), leading to repeatable and consistent setups. Option B (incorrect) is not an inherent, automatic benefit of IaC; while IaC can help implement cost-saving configurations, it doesn''t automatically optimize costs. Option C (incorrect) describes a function of monitoring tools (like Amazon CloudWatch), not a direct benefit of IaC itself. Option D (incorrect) is an indirect benefit at best; IaC focuses on infrastructure, not directly on application development or debugging.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  13,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_29',
  'What is a primary advantage of using Terraform for Infrastructure as Code (IaC) over manual provisioning?',
  'mcq',
  '["It allows for consistent and predictable infrastructure deployments.","It completely eliminates the need for cloud provider accounts.","It guarantees zero cost for all deployed resources.","It provides a visual drag-and-drop interface for infrastructure design."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is a primary advantage. IaC with Terraform ensures that infrastructure deployments are consistent and predictable because they are defined in code, reducing human error and configuration drift compared to manual provisioning. Option B (incorrect) is false; Terraform requires cloud provider accounts to provision resources. Option C (incorrect) is also false; Terraform manages resources that incur costs, it does not make them free. Option D (incorrect) is incorrect; Terraform is a command-line tool that uses HashiCorp Configuration Language (HCL), not a visual drag-and-drop interface.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  14,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_30',
  'When comparing Infrastructure as Code (IaC) with traditional manual infrastructure management, what is a key benefit of IaC regarding documentation?',
  'mcq',
  '["Infrastructure definitions serve as self-documenting code, providing an accurate record of the environment.","IaC eliminates the need for any external documentation, as everything is self-explanatory.","IaC automatically generates detailed user manuals for all deployed services.","IaC requires less documentation because changes are always visible in the cloud console."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) highlights ''documentation as code'' as a key benefit. The Terraform configuration files themselves serve as a precise and up-to-date documentation of the infrastructure, making it easier to understand, audit, and reproduce. Option B (incorrect) is an overstatement; while IaC improves documentation, some external documentation (e.g., architectural diagrams, design decisions) may still be beneficial. Option C (incorrect) is false; IaC does not automatically generate user manuals. Option D (incorrect) is a misconception; while changes are visible, the ''why'' and ''how'' are best captured in code and version control, not just the console.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  15,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
