  'mcq',
  '["Enhanced security auditing capabilities for compliance.","Improved resource tagging for cost allocation.","Repeatability, allowing consistent deployments across different environments or regions.","Reduced latency for end-users through optimized network routing."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is repeatability. IaC, particularly with Terraform, allows an organization to define its infrastructure once in code and then deploy it multiple times across different environments (e.g., development, staging, production) or geographical regions, ensuring each deployment is consistent and identical without manual errors. Option A (incorrect) is a security benefit that can be facilitated by IaC, but it''s not the primary benefit of deploying identical stacks. Option B (incorrect) is a management practice that can be automated with IaC, but it''s not the core benefit of consistent deployments. Option D (incorrect) relates to network performance, which is an outcome of infrastructure design, not a direct benefit of IaC''s provisioning model.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  21,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_37',
  'A company is migrating its manual infrastructure provisioning processes to Infrastructure as Code using Terraform. They aim to have a clear, human-readable record of their infrastructure''s design and current state, which can be easily shared and understood by new team members. Which IaC benefit is primarily being sought?',
  'mcq',
  '["Documentation as code, providing an up-to-date and executable record of infrastructure.","Automated compliance checks, ensuring adherence to regulatory standards.","Enhanced network security features, such as intrusion detection.","Real-time performance monitoring and alerting capabilities."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) refers to documentation as code. By defining infrastructure in Terraform''s HCL, the configuration files themselves serve as a precise, up-to-date, and executable documentation of the infrastructure. This is invaluable for onboarding new team members and understanding the current state of the environment. Option B (incorrect) is a benefit that can be integrated with IaC, but it''s not the primary benefit of the code itself serving as documentation. Option C (incorrect) and Option D (incorrect) are aspects of operational security and monitoring, respectively, which are distinct from the documentation benefit of IaC.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  22,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_38',
  'A critical application relies on a specific set of cloud resources. Over time, manual changes by different administrators have led to discrepancies between the documented infrastructure and its actual state. Which IaC benefit helps identify and rectify these unauthorized modifications?',
  'mcq',
  '["Automated cost reporting for resource usage.","Drift detection, by comparing the desired state with the actual infrastructure state.","Performance benchmarking for resource optimization.","Load balancing across multiple availability zones."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) describes drift detection. IaC tools like Terraform maintain a state file that represents the desired state of the infrastructure. By comparing this desired state with the actual state of the deployed resources, Terraform can detect ''drift'' – unauthorized or manual changes that have occurred outside of the IaC process. This allows teams to identify and rectify discrepancies, bringing the infrastructure back into alignment with the codified definition. Option A (incorrect) is a financial management aspect. Option C (incorrect) is about performance analysis. Option D (incorrect) is a networking feature, unrelated to detecting configuration changes.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  23,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_39',
  'A large enterprise needs to provision hundreds of virtual machines and networking components across multiple cloud providers for a new project. Manually performing these tasks would take weeks and be prone to human error. Which benefit of IaC with Terraform is most critical in this scenario?',
  'mcq',
  '["Increased auditability through detailed change logs.","Speed and efficiency, enabling rapid and automated provisioning at scale.","Enhanced security posture through automated vulnerability scanning.","Improved collaboration among development teams."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) highlights speed and efficiency. IaC allows for the rapid, automated provisioning of complex infrastructure at scale, significantly reducing the time and effort compared to manual processes, especially for large deployments involving hundreds of resources. Option A (incorrect) is a benefit of IaC, but speed is more critical when provisioning hundreds of resources quickly. Option C (incorrect) is a security practice that can be integrated, but not a direct benefit of IaC''s provisioning speed. Option D (incorrect) is also a benefit of IaC through version control, but the immediate and most impactful benefit for ''weeks'' of manual work is speed.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  24,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_40',
  'A company is experiencing frequent outages due to misconfigurations introduced during manual infrastructure updates. By adopting Terraform for IaC, they aim to minimize these errors. Which benefit of IaC is directly addressing this problem?',
  'mcq',
  '["Enhanced system performance through optimized resource allocation.","Reduced configuration errors, as changes are codified and automated.","Improved data encryption for sensitive information.","Simplified user authentication and authorization."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) directly addresses the problem of misconfigurations. IaC reduces configuration errors by codifying infrastructure, allowing changes to be tested, version-controlled, and automatically applied, minimizing human error associated with manual configuration. Option A (incorrect) is a goal of infrastructure design, not a direct benefit of IaC''s error reduction. Option C (incorrect) and Option D (incorrect) are security and identity management concerns, respectively, which are separate from the core benefit of reducing configuration errors through automation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  25,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_41',
  'A large organization needs to onboard new team members quickly, providing them with a clear understanding of the existing cloud infrastructure. Using Terraform for IaC contributes significantly to this by:',
  'mcq',
  '["Providing a visual drag-and-drop interface for infrastructure design.","Enabling the infrastructure definition to serve as up-to-date documentation.","Automatically generating detailed network diagrams from deployed resources.","Integrating directly with human resources systems for user provisioning."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) highlights the benefit of documentation as code. When infrastructure is defined in Terraform, the configuration files themselves act as a living, executable documentation of the infrastructure''s design and current state. This makes it much easier for new team members to understand the environment. Option A (incorrect) is not a feature of Terraform CLI. Option C (incorrect) is a capability that might be achieved with third-party tools, but not a direct benefit of Terraform''s core functionality. Option D (incorrect) is unrelated to infrastructure documentation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  26,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_42',
  'A security team requires a complete history of all infrastructure changes, including who made them, when, and what was changed, for auditing purposes. Which IaC benefit, when combined with a version control system, directly supports this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Automated resource tagging for cost management.","Auditability and traceability of infrastructure modifications.","Real-time threat detection and response capabilities.","Predictive analytics for resource capacity planning."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) directly addresses auditability and traceability. By managing Terraform configurations in a version control system like Git, every change to the infrastructure code is tracked, including the author, timestamp, and specific modifications. This provides a clear, auditable history of all infrastructure changes, which is crucial for compliance and security. Option A (incorrect) is for financial management. Option C (incorrect) is a security operations function. Option D (incorrect) is for capacity planning, not change tracking.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  27,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_43',
  'A software company needs to ensure that its production environment is always provisioned exactly the same way, regardless of who deploys it or when. They have experienced issues where manual deployments led to subtle differences between environments. How does Terraform, as an IaC tool, help solve this problem?',
  'mcq',
  '["By allowing engineers to manually adjust configurations during deployment for specific needs.","By enforcing consistency through codified configurations, ensuring identical deployments every time.","By providing a visual interface that guides users through manual setup steps.","By automatically optimizing resource allocation to reduce operational costs."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) explains how Terraform ensures consistency. By defining the desired infrastructure state in code, Terraform eliminates the variability of manual processes. Every deployment from the same configuration will result in an identical environment, ensuring consistency and preventing ''configuration drift'' caused by manual adjustments. Option A (incorrect) describes manual intervention, which IaC aims to reduce. Option C (incorrect) is not how Terraform primarily operates. Option D (incorrect) is a potential outcome of good IaC practices but not the direct mechanism for ensuring identical deployments.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  28,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_44',
  'A large e-commerce platform frequently launches new regional storefronts, each requiring an identical set of cloud infrastructure. Historically, this involved a lengthy manual process prone to human error. Using Terraform to automate this provisioning directly supports which IaC benefit?',
  'mcq',
  '["Reduced network latency for global users.","Enhanced data analytics capabilities.","Repeatability, enabling rapid and consistent deployment of identical environments.","Improved application performance through caching mechanisms."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is repeatability. For scenarios requiring identical infrastructure across multiple regions or environments, Terraform''s ability to define and deploy infrastructure from code ensures that each new storefront will have the exact same configuration, consistently and efficiently. Option A (incorrect) and Option D (incorrect) are performance benefits that might result from well-designed infrastructure, but not a direct benefit of IaC''s provisioning model. Option B (incorrect) relates to data processing, which is separate from infrastructure provisioning.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  29,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_45',
  'A company has multiple environments (development, staging, production) that should ideally be identical in terms of infrastructure. Over time, manual changes have caused these environments to diverge. Which IaC benefit, specifically with Terraform, helps detect and correct these discrepancies?',
  'mcq',
  '["Automated backup and restore capabilities for data.","Drift detection, by comparing the Terraform state with the actual cloud resources.","Centralized logging and monitoring of application performance.","Predictive analytics for future resource requirements."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) describes drift detection. Terraform maintains a state file that reflects the desired state of the infrastructure. By running `terraform plan` or `terraform apply`, Terraform compares this desired state with the actual state of the resources in the cloud. Any differences indicate ''drift,'' allowing the team to identify and rectify unauthorized or manual changes to bring environments back into alignment. Option A (incorrect) is a data management function. Option C (incorrect) is for observability. Option D (incorrect) is for capacity planning.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  30,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_46',
  'A new engineer joins a team that manages a complex cloud infrastructure using Terraform. They need to quickly understand the current infrastructure layout and its configuration details. Which benefit of IaC with Terraform directly assists in this onboarding process?',
  'mcq',
  '["Terraform''s ability to automatically generate detailed architectural diagrams.","The self-documenting nature of Terraform configurations, serving as an up-to-date infrastructure blueprint.","Terraform''s integration with advanced machine learning services for anomaly detection.","The built-in capabilities of Terraform to provide interactive training modules."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) refers to the self-documenting nature of Terraform configurations. The HCL files themselves serve as a clear, human-readable, and always up-to-date blueprint of the infrastructure. This ''documentation as code'' is invaluable for new team members to quickly grasp the infrastructure''s design and configuration. Option A (incorrect) is not a core feature of Terraform. Option C (incorrect) is unrelated to documentation. Option D (incorrect) is not a feature of Terraform.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  31,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_69_m_69_2_47',
  'A company needs to provision identical infrastructure for development, staging, and production environments. Each environment must be isolated but configured consistently. Which benefit of Infrastructure as Code (IaC) with Terraform is most relevant for this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["The ability to use the same codified configuration to repeatedly provision identical environments.","Automatic cost optimization by selecting the cheapest cloud providers for each environment.","Enhanced security through automated vulnerability scanning of deployed resources.","Real-time monitoring of application performance across all environments."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) highlights the repeatability and consistency benefits of IaC. By defining the infrastructure in Terraform, the same configuration can be applied to provision identical development, staging, and production environments, ensuring consistency and reducing configuration errors. Option B (incorrect) is not a direct or automatic benefit of IaC. Option C (incorrect) is a security practice that can be integrated but is not the primary benefit of consistent provisioning. Option D (incorrect) relates to operational monitoring, not the provisioning of identical environments.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain69_16',
  NOW(),
  32,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_69_2',
  'hard'
);

