  '{0}',
  'Option A (It downloads and installs the necessary provider plugins for the configuration) is a key action of `terraform init`. Terraform reads the configuration to identify required providers and then downloads their plugins into the `.terraform` directory. Option B (It authenticates with the cloud provider using configured credentials) is incorrect; `init` does not typically perform full authentication, though it might validate basic backend access. Authentication happens during `plan` and `apply`. Option C (It creates new provider configurations based on detected cloud resources) is incorrect; `init` uses existing configurations. Option D (It verifies the API connectivity to all declared cloud providers) is not the primary role of `init`; basic connectivity might be checked for the backend, but full API connectivity is tested during `plan` and `apply`.',
