  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) `terraform destroy` is the command used to safely delete all resources managed by the current Terraform configuration and state file. By default, `terraform destroy` will present a confirmation prompt before proceeding with the actual deletion, allowing the user to review the plan. Option B (`terraform apply -destroy`) is incorrect; while `terraform apply` can be used with a destruction plan (e.g., `terraform plan -destroy -out=planfile` then `terraform apply planfile`), `terraform destroy` is the dedicated command for this action. Options C (`terraform delete`) and D (`terraform remove`) are not valid Terraform CLI commands.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain71_16',
  NOW(),
  76,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_71_6',
  'hard'
);

