  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) `terraform destroy` is the command specifically designed to deprovision all resources managed by the current Terraform configuration and state file. By default, this command prompts for user confirmation before executing the destruction plan, providing a safety net. Option B (`terraform apply -destroy`) is not a direct command; a destruction plan would first need to be generated (e.g., `terraform plan -destroy -out=planfile`) and then applied. Options C (`terraform clean`) and D (`terraform remove`) are not valid Terraform CLI commands.',
