  'Option C (correct) `terraform fmt -check` is the correct command to check if Terraform configuration files are formatted correctly without modifying them. If any files are not compliant, the command will exit with a non-zero status code, which can be used to fail a CI/CD pipeline step. Option A (`terraform validate -format-check`) is incorrect; `terraform validate` does not check formatting. Option B (`terraform fmt --check-only`) is incorrect syntax; the correct flag is `-check`. Option D (`terraform style --verify`) is not a valid Terraform CLI command.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain71_16',
