  '{0}',
  'Option A (To rewrite Terraform configuration files to a canonical format and style) is the correct answer. `terraform fmt` automatically formats Terraform configuration files to a consistent, canonical style, which improves readability and maintainability, especially in team environments. Option B (To validate the syntax and internal consistency of Terraform configuration files) describes `terraform validate`. Option C (To download and install provider plugins and modules for a configuration) describes `terraform init`. Option D (To generate an execution plan showing proposed infrastructure changes) describes `terraform plan`.',
