INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_71_m_71_1_16',
  'A team wants to rename a resource in their Terraform configuration. After changing the resource block''s name, they need to update the state file to reflect this change without destroying and recreating the resource. Which `terraform state` subcommand should they use?',
  'mcq',
  '["`terraform state rm`","`terraform state pull`","`terraform state mv`","`terraform state push`"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is `terraform state mv`, which allows you to move a resource''s address in the state file, effectively renaming it or moving it to a different module path without destroying and recreating the actual infrastructure resource. Option A, `terraform state rm`, removes a resource from state. Options B and D are related to backend state manipulation, not renaming resources.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain71_16',
  NOW(),
  134,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_71_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_71_m_71_1_17',
  'A Terraform configuration uses `terraform workspaces` to manage ''dev'' and ''prod'' environments. How can the configuration reference the name of the currently selected workspace?',
  'mcq',
  '["Using the `terraform.environment` variable.","Using the `terraform.workspace` variable.","By manually setting an environment variable before running Terraform.","It cannot be referenced directly within the configuration."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) states that the `terraform.workspace` variable can be used within a Terraform configuration to reference the name of the currently selected workspace, allowing for environment-specific values or logic. Option A is incorrect; `terraform.environment` is not a standard built-in variable. Option C is a workaround but not the native Terraform way to reference the active workspace. Option D is incorrect.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain71_16',
  NOW(),
  135,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_71_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_71_m_71_1_18',
  'A company uses Terraform to manage its infrastructure. They are considering using `terraform workspaces` as the primary isolation mechanism between their production and development environments. Why is this generally considered an anti-pattern?',
  'mcq',
  '["Workspaces prevent the use of separate state backends for different environments.","Workspaces share the same code and provider configuration, increasing the risk of accidental cross-environment changes.","Workspaces introduce significant overhead, making deployments slower for production environments.","Workspaces are only designed for temporary, short-lived environments, not permanent ones."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) describes why using workspaces as the primary isolation mechanism for production and development is an anti-pattern. Workspaces share the same configuration code and provider settings, which can lead to accidental changes in one environment affecting another. For robust separation, separate Terraform root modules with distinct state backends and access credentials are recommended. Option A is incorrect; workspaces can use separate state backends. Option C is incorrect; workspaces don''t inherently slow down deployments. Option D is incorrect; workspaces can be used for permanent environments, but with the noted isolation limitations.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain71_16',
  NOW(),
  136,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_71_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_71_m_71_1_19',
  'Which command would you use to create a new workspace named ''staging''?',
  'mcq',
  '["`terraform workspace new staging`","`terraform create workspace staging`","`terraform workspace select staging`","`terraform init -workspace=staging`"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is the command `terraform workspace new staging`, which creates a new workspace named ''staging'' and automatically switches to it. Option B is not a valid Terraform command. Option C, `terraform workspace select staging`, would switch to an existing workspace, not create a new one. Option D is incorrect; `terraform init` does not create workspaces.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain71_16',
  NOW(),
  137,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_71_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
