  '["To define an unordered collection of unique string values.","To specify a structured data type with a fixed set of named attributes, each with its own type constraint.","To create a dynamic collection of key-value pairs where keys are integers.","To represent a simple list of values where order is the only concern."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) accurately describes the `object` type. An object allows you to define a schema for a complex variable, specifying exact attribute names and their expected types, ensuring structured data integrity. Option A describes a set of strings. Option C describes a map where keys are integers, which is not a standard map. Option D describes a list.',
