  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) `map(any)` is the most appropriate type. A `map` is a collection of key-value pairs where keys are strings, and values can be of any type, including other complex types. The `any` keyword allows for heterogeneous value types. Option A (incorrect) `list(string)` defines an ordered collection of string values, not key-value pairs. Option B (incorrect) `set(string)` defines an unordered collection of unique string values, also not key-value pairs. Option D (incorrect) `object({ key = string, value = any })` defines a structured type with predefined attributes (`key` and `value` in this example). While it can hold key-value information, it''s more rigid than a `map` if the keys themselves are dynamic and not known beforehand, and it forces a specific structure for each entry rather than a direct key-value mapping.',
