  'Option C (correct) `set(object({ ... }))` is the most appropriate type. A `set` ensures that all elements are unique and their order does not matter, which aligns with the requirement for unique rule objects where order is not important. Option A (incorrect) `list(object({ ... }))` would allow duplicate rule objects and imply an ordered collection, which is not desired. Option B (incorrect) `map(object({ ... }))` would require a unique string key for each rule object, which might not be natural for a collection of rules. Option D (incorrect) `tuple([object({ ... })])` defines a fixed-length list with specific types at each position, which is not suitable for a variable number of rules.',
