  'Option C (correct) `list(object({ ... }))` is the most appropriate type. A `list` is an ordered collection that allows duplicate elements. When combined with `object`, it allows you to define a list of structured configurations, where each element in the list is an object with specific attributes. This matches the requirement for an ordered collection of instance configurations where duplicates are allowed. Option A (incorrect) `set(object({ ... }))` would enforce uniqueness and disregard order. Option B (incorrect) `map(object({ ... }))` would require a unique string key for each object, and the order is not guaranteed. Option D (incorrect) `tuple` defines a fixed-length list with specific types at each position, which is not suitable for a variable number of instance configurations.',
