  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is the most appropriate type. A `list` allows for multiple interfaces, and each element of the list is an `object` that strictly defines the required attributes (`subnet_id`, `security_group_ids`, `primary`) and their respective types. This ensures structured, type-safe, and readable input. Option B (`map(string)`) is too simple; it cannot represent the complex structure needed for each interface. Option C (`set(string)`) and Option D (`list(string)`) are also too simple, as they cannot encapsulate multiple attributes per interface or enforce type safety for those attributes.',
