  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'Terraform supports managing multiple resource types within a single cloud provider by first having the Terraform configuration declare the specific cloud provider (Option B), such as `aws`. Terraform then uses a single provider plugin for that cloud (Option C) (e.g., the AWS provider). This provider exposes various resource types (Option A), such as `aws_instance` for EC2 or `aws_s3_bucket` for S3. Users then define various resources using the provider''s types (Option D) within their HCL configuration.',
