  '{2,3,0,1}',
  'Terraform''s provider model supports versioning by having the Terraform configuration specify a compatible provider version range (Option C) (e.g., `~> 3.0`). During `terraform init`, Terraform downloads the highest compatible provider version (Option D) within that range. Terraform then uses the specified provider version for resource management (Option A), ensuring consistent behavior. The provider developer releases new versions with API changes (Option B), and users update their version constraints to adopt them.',
