  '{0,2}',
  '`terraform fmt` focuses on code style and consistency. Option A (correct) by rewriting configuration files to a canonical format, `terraform fmt` ensures consistent code style, which significantly improves readability and maintainability for all team members. Option C (correct) consistent formatting helps reduce merge conflicts in version control systems, as changes are less likely to be purely stylistic. Option B (incorrect) `terraform fmt` does not correct syntax errors or validate resource configurations; that is the role of `terraform validate`. Option D (incorrect) `terraform fmt` has no impact on the optimization or speed of `terraform apply` operations. Option E (incorrect) `terraform fmt` does not resolve provider version conflicts; that is handled by `terraform init` and explicit version constraints.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain71_16',
