VALUES (
  'q_71_m_71_7_52',
  'Which of the following are common use cases for integrating `terraform fmt` into a CI/CD pipeline? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["To automatically format Terraform configuration files before committing to version control.","To ensure all pull requests adhere to a consistent coding style.","To validate the syntax and internal consistency of the configuration.","To generate a plan of infrastructure changes for review.","To destroy unformatted resources in the cloud environment."]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Integrating `terraform fmt` into CI/CD pipelines primarily serves to enforce code style. Option A (correct) `terraform fmt` can be run as a pre-commit hook or as part of a CI job to automatically format files, ensuring consistency before they are committed. Option B (correct) using `terraform fmt -check` in a CI/CD pipeline ensures that all pull requests (PRs) comply with the defined coding style, failing the build if any files are not correctly formatted. Option C (incorrect) validating syntax and internal consistency is the role of `terraform validate`, not `terraform fmt`. Option D (incorrect) generating a plan of infrastructure changes is done with `terraform plan`. Option E (incorrect) `terraform fmt` has no functionality related to destroying resources; that is handled by `terraform destroy`.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain71_16',
  NOW(),
  67,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_71_7',
  'medium'
);

