  'Option A (correct) is a primary benefit; `terraform fmt` automatically adjusts indentation and spacing to a canonical format, improving readability and consistency. Option C (correct) is also a key feature; it standardizes the order of arguments and blocks within a resource or data source, making configurations easier to read and compare. Option B (incorrect) is false; `terraform fmt` focuses on style, not syntax validation, which is handled by `terraform validate`. Option D (incorrect) is false; `terraform fmt` does not understand or correct logical errors; it only applies formatting. Option E (incorrect) is false; schema validation is part of `terraform validate` and `terraform plan`, not `terraform fmt`.',
