  '["`.tf` files (Terraform configuration files).","`.tfvars` files (Terraform variable definition files).","`.tfstate` files (Terraform state files).","`.gitignore` files (Git ignore files).","`.hcl` files (HashiCorp Configuration Language files)."]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (correct) and Option B (correct) are the primary file types that `terraform fmt` is designed to process. It applies canonical formatting to both `.tf` configuration files and `.tfvars` variable definition files. Option C (incorrect) `terraform fmt` does not modify `.tfstate` files; these are managed by `terraform init`, `plan`, `apply`, `destroy`, and `state` subcommands. Option D (incorrect) `terraform fmt` has no interaction with `.gitignore` files. Option E (incorrect) while Terraform uses HCL, `terraform fmt` specifically targets `.tf` and `.tfvars` files, not all generic `.hcl` files unless they are part of the Terraform configuration.',
