  'Which file types are typically processed by `terraform fmt` by default? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["`.txt` files containing general notes.","`.tf` files containing Terraform configuration.","`.md` files for documentation.","`.tfvars` files for variable definitions.","`.gitignore` files for version control exclusions."]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (correct) is true because `terraform fmt` is designed to format `.tf` files, which contain the core Terraform configuration. Option D (correct) is true as it also processes `.tfvars` files, which are used to define variable values, ensuring consistent formatting across all Terraform-related code. Options A, C, and E are incorrect as `terraform fmt` is specific to Terraform configuration files and does not process generic text, markdown, or version control configuration files.',
