  'Option C (correct) is the direct way to override a module''s default variable. You pass the desired value as an argument within the `module` block itself. Option A is incorrect; outputs are for values exposed by the module, not inputs. Option B is incorrect; defining a variable in the root module with a default value does not automatically pass it to a child module. Option D is incorrect; while `terraform.tfvars` can set root module variables, it doesn''t directly override a child module''s variable unless the root module explicitly passes that variable to the child.',
