  'Option C (correct) accurately describes the primary purpose of the `module` call block. It allows you to reuse a set of Terraform configurations (a module) by instantiating it with specific input variables. Option A is incorrect; `resource` blocks declare resources, and providers define resource types. Option B is incorrect; global variables are not a standard concept in Terraform in this way. Option D is handled by the `terraform` block''s `required_version` argument.',
