  'Option A (correct) is the standard way to specify a branch (or tag, or commit SHA) when sourcing from Git. You append `?ref=<BRANCH_NAME>` to the Git URL. Option B is incorrect; there is no `branch` argument for Git sources. Option C is incorrect; `version` is for registry modules or specific tags, not branch names in this context. Option D is incorrect; the default branch can be overridden.',
