  'Option A (correct) is a straightforward option. Storing a ZIP archive of the module in an Amazon S3 bucket (or similar cloud storage) and referencing it via an HTTP/HTTPS URL with the `http::` prefix allows easy sharing without complex setup. Option B (Terraform Registry public) is for public modules, not private team use. Option C (Local file paths) requires manual synchronization and is not scalable for a team. Option D (Bitbucket Cloud) is a valid Git source but might be more complex than a simple S3 bucket for a small team if they just need to share an archive.',
