  'Option C (correct) is the best option for hosting private, version-controlled modules internally. Private Git repositories (like GitHub Enterprise, GitLab, or Bitbucket) provide robust version control, access management, and integration with CI/CD pipelines for internal module development and consumption. Option A (public Terraform Registry) is for public modules. Option B (local filesystem paths) is suitable for modules within a single project but not for sharing across multiple projects or teams. Option D (HTTP URLs to public web servers) is generally not secure or manageable for private modules.',
