  'mcq',
  '["Local paths, referenced relative to the calling configuration.","Terraform Registry, for public sharing and discovery.","Git repositories, for external version-controlled dependencies.","Amazon S3 buckets, for remote, versioned archives."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) describes local paths. These are used when modules are part of the same repository or project, allowing them to be referenced by their file system path relative to the calling configuration. This is common for internal organization or during development before publishing. Option B is incorrect because the Terraform Registry is for sharing modules publicly or privately via Terraform Cloud/Enterprise. Option C is incorrect because Git repositories are typically used for external modules that are separate from the main configuration. Option D is incorrect because Amazon S3 buckets are used for remote, archived modules, often for private sharing or specific deployment scenarios, not typically for modules co-located within the same project.',
