  'What is the purpose of the `version` argument within a `module` block when sourcing from the Terraform Registry?',
  'mcq',
  '["To specify the desired version of the module to be downloaded and used.","To define the Terraform CLI version required for the module.","To indicate the API version of the cloud provider the module targets.","To set the version of the module''s internal variables."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is the purpose of the `version` argument. It allows you to specify which version of a module (e.g., from the Terraform Registry) Terraform should download and use, ensuring consistent deployments and preventing unexpected breaking changes. Option B is incorrect; the Terraform CLI version is specified in the `terraform` block''s `required_version`. Option C is incorrect; provider API versions are handled by provider configurations. Option D is incorrect; module variables do not have versions in this context.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain73_16',
