VALUES (
  'q_73_m_73_3_28',
  'A module is called `database_instance`. It has an output `instance_id`. How would you access this output in a `resource` block within the root module?',
  'mcq',
  '["`var.database_instance.instance_id`","`module.database_instance.instance_id`","`data.database_instance.instance_id`","`local.database_instance.instance_id`"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is the correct way to access an output from a child module. The syntax `module.<module_name>.<output_name>` is used to reference values exposed by a child module. Option A (`var.`) is for input variables to the current module. Option C (`data.`) is for data sources. Option D (`local.`) is for local values.',
