  '["Amazon EC2","AWS Lambda","Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon SQS"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is Amazon DynamoDB. When using the S3 backend, Terraform leverages a DynamoDB table to implement state locking, which prevents multiple users from concurrently modifying the state file and causing corruption. Option A, Amazon EC2, is for virtual servers. Option B, AWS Lambda, is for serverless compute. Option D, Amazon SQS, is a message queuing service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain74_16',
  NOW(),
  6,
