  'Option B (correct) is a significant limitation. The local backend stores the state file on the local filesystem and does not provide any mechanism for state locking or sharing, making it unsuitable for collaborative environments where multiple users might try to modify the infrastructure concurrently, leading to state corruption. Option A is incorrect; encryption is a separate concern. Option C is incorrect; there''s no such hard limit on resources for the local backend. Option D is incorrect; the local backend is typically faster for single-user operations than remote backends due to reduced network latency.',
