  'Option C (correct) is the primary reason. In a CI/CD pipeline, each build or job typically runs in an ephemeral environment. The local backend''s state file would be lost after the job completes, and it cannot be shared across multiple pipeline stages or concurrent builds, making it impossible to maintain a consistent view of the infrastructure. Option A is incorrect; Terraform is CLI-based. Option B is incorrect; Terraform is designed for automation. Option D is incorrect; while there are practical limits, it''s not the primary reason for CI/CD unsuitability.',
