  'Option B (correct) describes the purpose of the `terraform.tfstate.backup` file. Before Terraform writes a new state file after an `apply` operation, it saves the existing state file as `terraform.tfstate.backup`. This provides a simple local backup that can be used to recover if the latest state file becomes corrupted or if the `apply` operation introduced unintended changes. Option A (incorrect) state locking is not handled by this backup file. Option C (incorrect) sensitive information is stored in the main state file unless specifically redacted. Option D (incorrect) it''s a plain text (JSON) backup, not a compiled version.',
