  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) highlights the primary security concern with the local state file. Terraform state files, by default, store sensitive information (like database passwords, API keys, etc.) in plain text. If this file is not properly secured on the local filesystem, it can be a significant security vulnerability. Option A (incorrect) the local state file is not automatically encrypted by Terraform. Option C (incorrect) it is not automatically backed up to a public cloud service; only a local `.backup` file is created. Option D (incorrect) access depends on file permissions, not exclusively the root user.',
