  'For a targeted destruction, precision and verification are key. Option B (Execute `terraform init` to ensure the working directory is correctly configured) is the necessary first step to prepare the environment. Option C (Perform `terraform validate` to confirm the configuration is valid) should follow to catch any configuration errors. Option D (Generate a destroy plan for the targeted resource using `terraform plan -destroy -target=resource_type.resource_name`) is critical to preview *only* the destruction of the specified resource, ensuring no unintended resources are affected. Finally, Option A (Run `terraform destroy -target=resource_type.resource_name` and confirm interactively) executes the targeted destruction, with interactive confirmation providing a final safety check. Skipping the targeted plan review can lead to accidental deletion of incorrect resources or unintended dependencies.',
