  '{3,1,2,0}',
  'To generate and review a plan, you first modify the Terraform configuration files (Option D). Then, run `terraform init` to initialize the directory (Option B) if not already done. Next, execute `terraform plan` to generate the plan (Option C). Finally, review the proposed changes (add, change, destroy) (Option A) displayed in the output.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain71_16',
  NOW(),
  78,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_71_4',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_71_m_71_4_36',
  'Order the actions Terraform performs when you run `terraform plan`.',
  'ordering',
  '["Compare the desired state with the current real infrastructure state","Read the Terraform configuration files","Generate a detailed output of proposed changes","Fetch the current state of remote objects"]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'When running `terraform plan`, Terraform first reads the Terraform configuration files (Option B). Then, it fetches the current state of remote objects (Option D) from the cloud provider. Next, it compares the desired state (from config) with the current real infrastructure state (Option A). Finally, it generates a detailed output of proposed changes (Option C).',
