  'multiple',
  '["The Git repository URL, prefixed with `git::` (e.g., `git::https://github.com/org/repo.git`).","A specific Git reference (e.g., `?ref=v1.0.0` for a tag or `?ref=main` for a branch).","The AWS Region where the module''s resources will be deployed.","The full module address as it would appear in the public Terraform Registry.","A local file path relative to the root module''s directory."]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (correct) is the standard way to specify a Git repository as a module source, using the `git::` prefix. Option B (correct) is crucial for pinning the module to a specific version (tag), branch, or commit hash, ensuring consistent deployments. Option C (incorrect) is a configuration detail for the provider, not part of the module source itself. Option D (incorrect) is for modules hosted on the Terraform Registry, not Git repositories. Option E (incorrect) is for modules stored locally, not in a remote Git repository.',
