  '["The `source` argument will typically use a relative path (e.g., `./modules/my-module`).","The `source` argument can also use an absolute path (e.g., `/home/user/project/modules/my-module`).","Terraform will automatically download the module from the internet if it''s a local path.","A `version` argument is commonly used for local modules to manage updates.","The local module must be packaged as a `.zip` file for Terraform to recognize it."]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (correct) is the most common way to reference local modules, using a path relative to the calling configuration. Option B (correct) is also a valid way to specify a local module, though less common for portability. Option C (incorrect) is false; local modules are read directly from the filesystem, not downloaded. Option D (incorrect) is false; versioning is typically not applied to local modules in the same way it is for remote modules, as they are part of the same repository. Option E (incorrect) is false; local modules are simply directories containing `.tf` files, not `.zip` archives.',
